  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The size, scale, siting and design of the proposed development, would present a disproportionately sized dwelling, which would extend abutting the west boundary, closing the openness of the plot resulting in the loss of the spatial quality of the streetscene whilst also failing to incorporate the architectural features of the dwellings in the area. The dwelling would therefore be out of character with the area and harm the appearance of the streetscene. As such, the proposal is considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:Paragraphs 131 and 135 of the National Planning Policy Framework (December 2023)Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy CP3 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010)Policy BP11 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policies SP2, DMD1, and DMD6 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan (Regulation 19 Main Modifications Version, December 2021)"
  ],
